QUERY (a symptom-level bug report):
A team event that mixes hosts who are always on the invitation with a rotating pool of others can still be booked at a moment when nobody from that pool is free, because only the always-present hosts are checked. The booking is taken and then falls over afterwards, and what comes back to the caller is a generic failure that never says which condition was not met.

